# C# code style (CherryPlay)

## Three layers (server)

Keep CherryPlayServer as **Controller → Service → Repository**:

| Layer | Lives in | Responsibility |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Controllers** | `Controllers/` | HTTP only: bind/validate input shape, auth attributes, map to/from DTOs, status codes. **No** business rules, **no** DbContext/EF. |
| **Services** | `Core/Services/` (+ `Core/Interfaces/` for ports) | Business logic, invariants, orchestration, transactions across repos. Return domain/result types — not `IActionResult`. |
| **Repositories** | `Infrastructure/Repositories/` (+ EF under `Infrastructure/Persistence/`) | Persistence only: load/save entities. **No** product rules (e.g. which document types are “required”). |

- Controllers depend on **services** (or narrow application ports), not on repositories directly (except rare read-only admin escapes — prefer avoid).
- Services depend on **repository interfaces** in `Core/Interfaces/`; implementations in Infrastructure.
- Naming: `IFooRepository` / `InMemoryFooRepository` / `EfFooRepository` — avoid parallel names like Store/Registry for the same persistence port.
- Domain rules that look like “policy” (required consent types, one-active-per-type publish) belong in **services** (or a dedicated domain service), not in repository filters — unless the rule is a pure storage constraint documented as such.

## One type per file

- **One** `class`, `struct`, `enum`, or `interface` per `.cs` file (file name = type name).
- **Exception:** `record` DTOs and small request/response types may share a file when they belong to one API surface (e.g. `LegalDtos.cs`, `AuthResult` next to its interface only if the interface is alone — prefer split when a second class appears).
- **Not allowed:** helper `static` class + test harness + stub in one file; nested private classes in production code — extract to own file.
- Test doubles (`*Stub`, `*Harness`, `*TestFactory`) — each in its own file under `CherryPlayServer.Tests/`.

```csharp
// ❌ LegalConsentTestHelper.cs — helper + harness + stub
internal static class LegalConsentTestHelper { }
internal sealed class LegalOAuthHarness { }

// ✅ LegalConsentTestHelper.cs + LegalOAuthHarness.cs
```

## Namespaces

- `file-scoped namespace` matching folder layer: `CherryPlayServer.Core.*`, `Infrastructure.*`, etc.

## Usings

- No blank line between every `using`; single block at top.

## Collection return types

- For collection contracts in interfaces, public services, and read models, use read-only interfaces instead of mutable types such as `List<T>`.
- Use `IReadOnlyList<T>` when ordering or indexed access is part of the contract; use `IReadOnlyCollection<T>` when neither matters.
- A read-only interface limits what callers can do through that reference; it does not make a mutable backing collection immutable. Avoid returning a mutable `List<T>` behind a read-only interface. Where practical, return immutable collections or a read-only wrapper over a private materialized array.
- Keep mutable collections local to implementations when needed, and copy or wrap them before crossing a read-only boundary.

## When adding types

- New interface → new file under `Core/Interfaces/`.
- New EF entity + configuration → separate files in `Persistence/Entities` and `Configurations/`.
- Implementation of an interface → dedicated class file (no “hidden” second interface on an existing class unless it is the single implementation and registered explicitly in DI).
